{
	title: 'Byte limit for source files with a pre-commit hook',
	spec: 'Files under src/ matching *.ts or *.tsx, tests included, stay at or under 20,000 bytes (about 5,000 tokens at bytes / 4) so an agent can read each whole. Bytes replace the 450-line limit because line counts depend on formatting: oxfmt raised them by 40% without growing the code. scripts/size-limit.ts holds the limit, exceptions with reasons (common/ason.ts: self-contained) and splitting advice: move one coherent responsibility into a module named for it, without re-exports; split tests by feature area into <module>-<area>.test.ts with shared fixtures in a helper; never shrink by squeezing formatting or deleting comments or tests. conventions.test.ts checks all of src/. scripts/hooks/pre-commit checks only staged files and prints the advice; package.json prepare sets core.hooksPath on bun install.',
